# Build output
build/
# Generated screenshots, profiling captures and local release verification.
# These are useful working artifacts, but reproducible and often very large.
artifacts/
*.exe
*.o
*.obj
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Browser build output. web/index.html IS tracked -- it is the page. What sits
# beside it is compiler output: the Pages workflow rebuilds both from src/ on
# every deploy, so committing a 20 MB wasm would only add a large binary to
# every diff that could disagree with the source it came from.
web/cinderlift.js
web/cinderlift.wasm
web/*.wasm.map
web/*.data

# Saved games -- yours, not the repository's
*.sav

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local cross-agent implementation journal. It is intentionally untracked:
# public mechanics belong in the repository docs, while this holds the current
# work state and handoff notes for the people/agents working in this checkout.
HANDOFF.md

# Wrangler's local cache. It holds the Cloudflare account id and the account
# name (an email address), neither of which belongs in a public repository --
# and none of which any build needs. Ignored rather than remembered.
.wrangler/
signal/.wrangler/
